    "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired using a BrainAmp system (BrainProducts GmbH) with 60 channels at 250 Hz sampling rate, referenced to FCz with Fpz as ground. Subjects performed cue-based motor imagery of three right-arm grasping tasks in three sessions separated by 7 days. Each trial consisted of a 3 s rest period, 3 s visual cue, and 4 s motor imagery window. Data were preprocessed with 60 Hz notch filtering and cue-aligned epoching.",
